course: dictionary
lesson: 9977
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words look and sound the same but mean different things. The context tells you which meaning is right. Tear can mean a drop of water from your eye, or to pull something apart. Say a tear (rhymes with «ear») for the drop from your eye, and to tear (rhymes with «air») for ripping.
explain: «At home Alfie took one look at the bruise and burst into tears.» Here tears are the drops from his eyes, because bursting into tears means starting to cry. «Metal rivets stopped pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.» Here tearing means pulling apart, because a pocket can rip.
explain: Ask yourself: do the other words in the sentence talk about eyes and feelings, or about pulling and ripping? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it makes sense. Tear can also mean to move very fast, as in «tear along the path». Read on before you decide.
fact: A tear (rhymes with «ear») is a drop of salty water from your eye.
fact: To tear (rhymes with «air») means to pull something apart or make a hole in it.
fact: «In tears» means crying, and «burst into tears» means suddenly starting to cry.
fact: Tears clean and protect your eyes and wash out dust.
fact: «Tears of joy» are tears you cry when you feel very happy.
exercise: In «Alfie took one look at the bruise and burst into tears», what are the tears? | Pieces of paper pulled apart | *Drops of water from his eyes | Something moving very fast | A hole in his shirt
exercise: In «Metal rivets stopped pockets tearing on miners' work trousers», what does tearing mean? | Making a loud noise | Running very fast | *Pulling apart or ripping | Crying
exercise: Ruby says, «I will tear this paper into pieces for my collage.» What does tear mean? | *To pull apart | A drop of water from the eye | To move very fast | A happy feeling
test: Grandma says, «Please don't tear the page out of the library book.» What does tear mean? | A happy feeling | *To rip or pull apart | A drop of water from the eye | To run very fast
test: Mia cried tears of joy when she won the race. What does tears of joy mean? | Crying because she hurt her knee | A hole in her shirt | Running very fast | *Crying because she was very happy
exam: Jake tore along the path to get home before the rain. What does tore mean here? | Pulled apart | Cried | *Moved very fast | Made a hole in his coat
